# Detailed Implementation Blueprint: Candidate Identity & Session History Manager

This document provides the step-by-step technical plan to implement **Component 1: Candidate Identity & Session History Manager** in your backend without changing any code today.

---

## 🎯 Objectives & Scope

The **Candidate Identity & Session History Manager** solves two main problems:
1. **Name Resolution**: Maps candidate names (e.g. `"Samiksha"`) to their system `user_id` (e.g. `"2071"`).
2. **Session Discovery & Chronological Sorting**: Scans S3/ChromaDB for all interview sessions of a given `user_id`, sorts them by `session_start_time`, and retrieves the candidate's latest $N$ interviews (e.g., last 3 interviews).

